From: MacSW maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Serialise empty elements with an explicit end tag, as native MSXML does.

Native MSXML writes an empty element as "<tag></tag>", never as the
self-closing form "<tag/>" that node_dump() produced. The SOLIDWORKS Activation
Wizard computes the <CheckSum> of its request over the MSXML (expanded)
serialisation but writes the request with this routine, so the saved request
differed from the checksummed form and the licensing server answered
"Bad Checksum". Emit "<tag></tag>" for an element without children.

diff --git a/dlls/msxml3/node.c b/dlls/msxml3/node.c
--- a/dlls/msxml3/node.c
+++ b/dlls/msxml3/node.c
@@ -2051,7 +2051,18 @@
             node_dump_element_attributes(context, node);
             if (list_empty(&node->children))
             {
-                node_dump_append(context, L"/>", 2);
+                /* Native MSXML always serialises an empty element with an
+                 * explicit start/end tag pair ("<tag></tag>"), never the XML
+                 * self-closing form ("<tag/>") that libxml2-style writers use.
+                 * SOLIDWORKS' Activation Wizard computes the request <CheckSum>
+                 * over the MSXML (expanded) serialisation but writes the file
+                 * with this routine; emitting "<tag/>" makes the saved request
+                 * differ from the checksummed form, so Dassault's activation
+                 * server rejects it as "edited or incomplete".  Match MSXML. */
+                node_dump_append(context, L">", 1);
+                node_dump_append(context, L"</", 2);
+                node_dump_qualified_name(context, node);
+                node_dump_append(context, L">", 1);
             }
             else
             {
